mantle rm461
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_una_rustridge
title the latch with the cough
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=nervy talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk catches_a_cough_in_the_rattle_of_a_latch
likes warm_bread wrestling festival_bells autumn_wind
dislikes smoke gulls
fears letting_a_door_blow_back_on_an_unsteady_foot
hopes for_a_quiet_place_beside_a_warm_bread_board
topics work +0.4 health +0.3 animals +0.1 pastimes +0.2 weather +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=curt refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# clears a rough throat under the clatter of a latch and knows how hard to pull a door against an autumn gust.

words
oath! = Rattle my latch twice | By the stubborn hinge
saying! = A latch can have the last cough | Mind the foot behind the door
latch = a loose latch tongue | the brass latch
hook = the retaining hook | a short latch hook
wedge = my door wedge | a wooden shoe for the door
bread = a steaming bread end | a hot heel
sound = the clack of iron | a hollow rattle
air = the cold bit of air | a draught off the stones
cloth = a clean neck cloth | my soft kitchen rag
roll = a crisp brown roll | a small warm bun
bell = the middle bell | a big low feast bell
grit = grit in the hinge | the gritty fleck
gull = a loud grey gull | a hungry white bird
hip = a sideways hip turn | my short wrestling turn

any
opinion houses against 2 : Fine timber for a grand door. What I'd like to know is whether it opens to the wolves who carried the boards there.
opinion merchants against 2 : A warm bread smell comes out free. I've been obliged to make do with the smell on more than one afternoon.
opinion dole for 2 : Soup got past my throat when a dry crust wouldn't, one lean week. I'll give the ladle that much credit.
opinion times against 2 : There's a little less coming in through my own door each week. The draught's as generous as ever.
opinion festivals against 1 : The bells please me. I appreciate all the qualities of the crowd from a considerable distance.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Come inside the swing. Welcome. | There's room near the quiet hinge.
line greet [self.working=yes] : One ear free at the door. | I can hear before the latch goes down.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : No other sound this early but the click. | Morning. The door's in a decent temper.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening brings a slower foot over the sill. | Late light fits under the door.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin can stand beside my own latch hand. | A familiar sound against the wood.
line again.open : Back before the hinge has cooled. | There's our second little rattle.
line greet.return : Heard you. No knock needed. | Yes. I can look up now.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I'd pick your step out under a heavy door. | That sound's welcome on my sill.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Speak while I keep the door from swinging. | I've got the weight of it. Go ahead.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I can see a little by the crack. | The quiet hinge leaves room for a greeting.
line farewell : Take the gap before the wind claims it. | May your own latch lift easily.
line farewell.return : I'll put the hook back after you. | Keep your tail clear of the moving bit.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : A quiet hinge at the dark end of the street. | Good footing under the last sill.
line react.news : Which part came clearly through the door? | Speak above the little rattle.
line react.news.new : That's a different knock altogether. | News from a hinge I haven't heard.
line react.news.known : Already lifted the latch on that bit. | I know which way that story opens.
line react.news.doubt : There may be loose iron in that account somewhere. | I'd listen once more without a door rattling in between.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Sit on the warm side with me. | Poor news. I'll keep the draught away.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good news comes in almost silently. | A pleasant caller, that account.
line ask.how : How has the draught been treating you? | Anything caught in the hinge of your day?
line answer.how : A quieter throat than my latch would suggest. | Doing tolerably well at keeping the door steady.
line decline : I'd sooner keep my place out of the draught. | I need a little rest in easier air today.
line accept_decline : Clear enough. I can let that close. | The hook need never come loose.
line thank : You've saved me a hard push. | I'll remember the paw on the door.
line sympathise : Take my sheltered angle and your time. | I'll hold the awkward part still.
line reassure : A door can wait till your breathing comes easy. | Most rattles settle if you keep your paw steady.
line preclose : My latch wants another look before long. | I should move back to the opening now.

scene cough
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If the latch makes a noise while I clear my throat, that's its affair.
b : Which was the latch? | Do you need a little water?
a : That's rather the virtue of a good loose fitting. Not always easy to say. | A little would be welcome. Purely for general comfort, naturally.

scene door
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I listen for the hinge to say when a gust has taken the weight.
b : What does it say? | Can you hold it then?
a : A creak changes to a sigh. That's when the door will start to help itself. | With the foot wedge. My poor shoulder has no desire to wrestle an entire street.

scene bread
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take warm bread where the skin has pulled away from the crumb.
b : Why that bit? | Does it cool fast?
a : There's a pocket of steam there that smells like another whole loaf. | Naturally. That's my excellent reason for proceeding without further delay.

scene grip
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd take a good wrestler's stance for holding a door.
b : What does a door weigh? | Which stance?
a : Depends on the wind behind it. A small door can take on ideas well above its timber. | Feet apart, one slightly back, no stiff arm to jolt when the wind changes.

scene bells
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like feast bells once the lower one has joined in.
b : Why wait? | Can you tell which bell?
a : The first shrill notes sound like somebody finding a bent hinge. The low bell makes a tune of them. | From inside a shut room the lowest note continues right down through the floor.

scene autumn
when topic=season self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a good autumn wind coming squarely up the street.
b : Even on your door? | Why squarely?
a : Keeps me properly employed. And afterwards the room knows it has a fresh supply of air. | A side gust is always bargaining with the hinge. Give me an honest push.

scene smoke
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke meeting me in a doorway always gets the opening word.
b : What do you say back? | Can you turn it aside?
a : Several elaborate noises best attributed to the latch. | Sometimes. A door held at the right angle can send the worst of it past the sill.

scene gulls
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull can find a gap barely wider than a crust.
b : Inside the house? | Does a good latch help?
a : At least the head comes in. The rest is an argument with wings. | More than a polite explanation ever did.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can offer #self.friend# a place where the warm air comes past before the cold.
b : Is that such a fine offer? | Where is it?
a : It feels fine to a tired throat and costs me only a shift of my feet. | Behind the swing, a step out from the jamb. Try it and see.

scene worry
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't move my foot wedge until I see the last foot clearly.
b : What if the visitor lingers? | Is it heavy?
a : Then the wedge and I linger too. A stiff door needn't have an opinion about anybody's pace. | My wedge? No. The timber it's keeping polite has a good deal of weight to it.

scene sump
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A Sump door keeps out half a street with surprisingly little timber.
b : Isn't that lonely? | What about the noise?
a : One wants a little street left outside. I still lift the latch for the rest. | That gets in with the air unless I've stuffed the bad corner with a rag.

scene steps
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave room for whoever comes out of a doorway carrying something wide.
b : Isn't that just manners? | Even in a hurry?
a : Yes. Fine thing manners. Saves a fine amount in broken crockery. | A basket lodged against my middle slows my journey more.

scene fee
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I reckon warmth into the price I pay for a bread roll.
b : Quite a lot extra? | Do you go far to get one?
a : Very little extra to the seller, a considerable difference to me. | Not past the distance where it turns into an ordinary cold roll on the return.

scene tell
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep talk overheard through an open door instead of passing it down the street.
b : What's the use of hearing it? | Even some good news?
a : It tells me whether an arrival could use a chair. I need no more than that. | A good word ought to arrive by the door its owner chooses.

scene body
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A torn bit of ear is a precise instrument for telling which way a draught goes.
b : Does it hurt? | How precise?
a : Only when the cold gets under the fur. I turn the undamaged side towards the breeze. | Right down to the loose board that was supposed to keep the wind outside.

scene listen
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a stranger room to ask before reaching over the sill.
b : And a caller with a soft voice? | To protect the goods?
a : I lean a little. The weight of a door is enough intimidation without a great bellow to go with it. | To protect my footing. An unexpected elbow can go anywhere.

scene tight
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean day makes me more conscious of the small coins that roll under doors.
b : Would you keep one? | Can you hear it go?
a : If I know the owner, I'd rather get it back to the right pocket. I've done shopping one copper short. It teaches a precise value. | A thin little roll quite unlike a boot scrabbling in grit.

scene hingedream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt the whole city was a door opening gently into another city.
b : What lay through it? | Who had the key?
a : Another set of doors, to my concern. I had been hoping for an end to the work. | I was getting to that particular anxiety when the morning started.

story hingeoil [topic=memories]
  : One evening I oiled a hinge so well I kept turning my head at the wrong moment to see who had come inside. The whole door made less noise than my neck cloth.
  : The next afternoon I left just a little click in the latch. I wanted a warning with decent manners, not a door with no voice at all.
  b : Did the door keep quiet?
  : It gave exactly the little click I needed. If only a wolf could be adjusted with equal ease.

story breadflight [topic=food]
  : I once drove off a gull by holding my warm bread high under my coat, but a bit of loose crust caught on the button. The gull came round for that.
  : I found myself wearing a very small brown flag. I took the button out of consideration by eating the flag myself.
  b : Did the gull leave?
  : After inspecting my other buttons very thoroughly. I've had less determined customers.

story wedgework [topic=work self.job=merchant]
  : I tried using a small book to prop a door open. It was a perfectly bad book about efficient ways of packing things, almost exactly the right thickness.
  : The bindings were much too smooth. The door crept quietly across the floor with the book still underneath, as if carrying it off to read in private.
  b : What did you do?
  : Made a wedge from rough wood. The book now addresses the more practical subject of steadying a table leg.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Hook fast before anybody crosses. | Mind the second foot behind the first.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.dislikes=smoke
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Turn the loose air away from the sill. | The latch can explain that little rattle.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Fold the crust inside before the heat gets out. | A hot heel for the quiet side.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.season=autumn
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Wide stance for a long bit of wind. | That draught's a lively little wrestler.

dlg resident.hub : Stand beyond the latch's turning circle. It's simpler to conduct a conversation when the door hasn't taken hold of your coat.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I keep people and parcels on speaking terms with the hinge.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This bit came in with a very clear knock. #world.news#
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, the latch hasn't lost the sound of you.
dlg resident.bye : Leave the heavy part of the door to me.

graft resident.hub
choice Which noise is the door and which one is you? -> latch_noise
node latch_noise
say The deep clatter is the door if I'm standing a good way off. When I'm nearer, the two of us benefit from a little modest uncertainty.
free
choice Would oil solve the problem? -> latch_oil
choice A courteous sort of latch. -> hub
node latch_oil
say For the hinge. For me a mouthful of water would be quite as practical. Small attentions suited to the particular case.
choice I'll remember the water. -> hub
choice I'll leave the hinge to you. -> bye
